From: Rob Vogelaar <revogelaar@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ap: defer WDS-STA setup in ieee802_11_rx_from_unknown until authorized

Companion to 0003: the 4-address WDS STA netdev is also created from
ieee802_11_rx_from_unknown() on the first 4-addr frame (M2), before the 4-way. On
mac80211_hwsim that diverts the STA's pre-auth EAPOL (M4) to the WDS netdev instead
of the authenticator, so the 4-way times out (reason 15). Mark WLAN_STA_WDS early
(so ap_sta_set_authorized() has a trigger) but defer the netdev creation until the
station is AUTHORIZED.
---
--- a/source/hostap-2.11/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/source/hostap-2.11/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -7325,18 +7325,25 @@
 		}
 
 		if (wds && !(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_WDS)) {
-			int ret;
-			char ifname_wds[IFNAMSIZ + 1];
-
-			wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "Enable 4-address WDS mode for "
-				   "STA " MACSTR " (aid %u)",
-				   MAC2STR(sta->addr), sta->aid);
+			/* meta-cmf-bananapi-vcpe: mark the STA as 4-address (preserve state) but defer
+			 * creating/enslaving the WDS netdev until it is AUTHORIZED. Creating it now -- on
+			 * the first 4-addr frame (typically M2) -- makes mac80211_hwsim route the STA's
+			 * pre-auth EAPOL (M4) to the WDS netdev before the authenticator receives it, so
+			 * the 4-way times out (reason 15). ap_sta_set_authorized() creates it on auth. */
 			sta->flags |= WLAN_STA_WDS;
-			ret = hostapd_set_wds_sta(hapd, ifname_wds,
+			if (sta->flags & WLAN_STA_AUTHORIZED) {
+				int ret;
+				char ifname_wds[IFNAMSIZ + 1];
+
+				wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "Enable 4-address WDS mode for "
+					   "STA " MACSTR " (aid %u)",
+					   MAC2STR(sta->addr), sta->aid);
+				ret = hostapd_set_wds_sta(hapd, ifname_wds,
 						  sta->addr, sta->aid, 1);
-			if (!ret)
-				hostapd_set_wds_encryption(hapd, sta,
+				if (!ret)
+					hostapd_set_wds_encryption(hapd, sta,
 							   ifname_wds);
+			}
 		}
 		return;
 	}
